@startuml auth-service
title auth-service — src/

package "cpp-httplib" {
  class "httplib::Server" as HttplibServer
}

package "nlohmann-json / OpenSSL" {
  class "nlohmann::json" as Json
  class "HMAC-SHA256" as Hmac
}

namespace base64_utils {
  class base64_utils <<namespace>> {
    +{static} encodeUrl(data: vector<uint8_t>) : string
    +{static} decodeUrl(text: string) : vector<uint8_t>
  }
}

class Token {
  +value : string
  +expiresAt : int64
}

class TokenService {
  +issueToken(subject: string) : Token
  +verifyToken(token: string) : optional<string>
  +issueRefreshToken(subject: string) : Token
  +verifyRefreshToken(token: string) : optional<string>
  -issueTokenInternal(subject: string, ttl: seconds, isRefresh: bool) : Token
  -verifyTokenInternal(token: string, expectRefresh: bool) : optional<string>
}
TokenService ..> Token : creates
TokenService ..> Hmac : signs/verifies with
TokenService ..> Json : encodes payload as
TokenService ..> base64_utils.base64_utils : uses

class UserServiceClient {
  +verifyCredentials(login: string, password: string) : bool
  +registerUser(login: string, password: string) : bool
}
UserServiceClient ..> "user-service" : POST /users/verify-credentials,\nPOST /users/register

class HttpServer {
  +listen(host: string, port: int)
  +stop()
  -handleIssueToken(request, response)
  -handleVerifyToken(request, response)
  -handleRegister(request, response)
  -handleRefresh(request, response)
}
HttpServer --> TokenService : delegates to (const&)
HttpServer --> UserServiceClient : checks credentials via (const&)
HttpServer *-- HttplibServer : owns

note right of HttpServer
  Routes:
  POST /auth/token    -> handleIssueToken
                         (verifies login/password via
                         UserServiceClient first)
  POST /auth/verify   -> handleVerifyToken
  POST /auth/register -> handleRegister
                         (forwards to user-service, then
                         issues a token immediately on
                         success — auto-login)
  POST /auth/refresh  -> handleRefresh (issue #105)
                         exchanges a still-valid
                         refresh_token for a fresh
                         access token, no credentials
                         needed again

  /auth/token and /auth/register now also
  return a long-lived refresh_token
  alongside the access token
  (TokenService::issueRefreshToken()).
  Refresh tokens carry "typ": "refresh"
  in their payload so they can never be
  used as an access token (or vice
  versa) even though both share the
  same signing secret — see
  TokenService's doc comment.
end note

@enduml
